# ================================
# BLANKET SLICE, STAGE L2P: L2 PHYSICS (FIRST-WALL FLUX + NUCLEAR HEATING)
# IN PHYSICAL TIME WITH A PLASMA PULSE
#   PHYSICS  : AS blanket_L2.par (WATER 0.050 kg/s, 298.15 K; EUROFER97;
#              BC 532 1.0e5 W/m2; Q = 1.6e6 exp(-d / 0.15 m) W/m3 IN THE STEEL)
#   PULSE    : BOTH HEAT SOURCES ARE MULTIPLIED BY f(t) FROM THE TABLE IN
#              CBS3D_HEAT_PULSE_FILE (DEFAULT pulse_600s.txt; HeatPulse.hpp)
#   TIME     : transient_on = 1, ONE GLOBAL TIME STEP (ilots = 0, ~4.4e-4 s
#              AT h4); STOPS AT end_rtime = 600 s
#   START    : THE CONVERGED L2 FIELD OF A STEADY ENERGY RUN (E.G. 30102) AS
#              THE INITIAL CONDITION AT t = 0 (blanket.sh pulse RUN_DIR)
#   OUTPUT   : ONE .pvtu EVERY 5 s OF PHYSICAL TIME (vtu_output_every_sim_time)
#              AND AT THE END; PROBES AND REGULAR-GRID SAMPLES FROM
#              PointSampler (blanket.sh pulse SETS THEM)
# LINES STARTING WITH # ARE COMMENTS.
# ================================
